{"id":"baal-zebub","name":"Baal-Zebub","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:baal-zebub"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Baal-zebub","text":"Fly-lord, the god of the Philistines at Ekron (2 Kings 1:2, 3, 16). This name was given to the god because he was supposed to be able to avert the plague of flies which in that region was to be feared. He was consulted by Ahaziah as to his recovery."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1176","lemma":"בַּעַל זְבוּב","xlit":"Baʻal Zᵉbûwb","gloss":"Baal-Zebub, a special deity of the Ekronites","kjv":"Baal-zebub","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H6138","lemma":"עֶקְרוֹן","xlit":"ʻEqrôwn","gloss":"Ekron, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Ekron","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H1875","lemma":"דָּרַשׁ","xlit":"dârash","gloss":"to tread or frequent","kjv":"ask, at all, care for, diligently","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H4397","lemma":"מֲלְאָךְ","xlit":"mălʼâk","gloss":"a messenger","kjv":"ambassador, angel, king, messenger","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H4296","lemma":"מִטָּה","xlit":"miṭṭâh","gloss":"a bed forsleeping or eating","kjv":"bed, bier","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","xlit":"Shômᵉrôwn","gloss":"Shomeron, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Samaria","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["2Kgs.1.2","2Kgs.1.3","2Kgs.1.6","2Kgs.1.16"],"related":[{"id":"elijah","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.025,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ashdod","type":"lexical","strong":"H6138","why":"both lead with עֶקְרוֹן (H6138)"},{"id":"ashkelon","type":"lexical","strong":"H6138","why":"both lead with עֶקְרוֹן (H6138)"},{"id":"ekron","type":"lexical","strong":"H6138","why":"both lead with עֶקְרוֹן (H6138)"}],"works":[{"work":"kebra","title":"Kebra Nagast","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Kebra.60","count":1,"book":"Kebra N.","title":"Solomon’s Lament for the Tabernacle of Zion"}]}]}
